{"id": "EUVD-2026-86706", "enisaUuid": "f397fcbe-b368-3adf-a121-a7e4d6c2736a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: Intel: avs: Refactor and fix init_config access\n\nExisting code accesses enties found in ->init_configs array through\nindexes that are part of ->config_ids array.  Those two are limited by:\n->num_init_configs and ->num_config_ids respectively.  Using ID larger\nor equal to ->num_init_configs leads to out-of-bounds access:\n\navs_path_module_send_init_configs()\nloop:\n\t(...) &acomp->tplg->init_configs[ids[i]]\n\t\t\t\t\t^ out-of-bounds candidate\n\nRather than adding another if-statement, refactor the code.  There is no\nneed to store the IDs, have a list of pointers to actual config-entries\ninstead.  As the verification of ->init_config entries does not differ from\nverification of other types that are part of the topology.c file, simply\nreuse the code.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70ffcaf86a053be99daaf3b103beac0ad7136ca3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75bd5ea9c858d89fb8862f23afb00783bf02cd7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f20a0f4f7d638e83ae86db1719a24c7049762f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/681e91035dc794896a904852040837190e5041f5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98053", "GHSA-xpmc-f98f-h67j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "24d4617c-bb15-3d53-b9c6-8eb46cf2920d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a49ef789b1be68242624d460df2ada8087308a7 <681e91035dc794896a904852040837190e5041f5"}, {"id": "336bed66-b9fe-3783-a697-ce48a22e2a22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a49ef789b1be68242624d460df2ada8087308a7 <70ffcaf86a053be99daaf3b103beac0ad7136ca3"}, {"id": "34944ca8-784f-323f-88ba-9960bd98a62d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "52355c86-7f33-321c-ab0b-2de4b9f09baa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a49ef789b1be68242624d460df2ada8087308a7 <75bd5ea9c858d89fb8862f23afb00783bf02cd7a"}, {"id": "8950f2ac-1770-3d83-9de4-69839214de9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "9d1253b5-43b2-3ef4-a188-34258a7c4d9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "9eba15aa-8059-35c2-8375-5ae7afaaa411", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "b7b2650e-48b3-33e7-a41c-76a5ff1bb7d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "bfe3cce8-f426-3507-860a-bb39ec4adc68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e64673f6-591d-30dd-acf2-39e8d813329c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a49ef789b1be68242624d460df2ada8087308a7 <8f20a0f4f7d638e83ae86db1719a24c7049762f5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "db119a47-2098-3fe0-bfaa-4b79a77a8211", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}